<div class="tab-content" id="archTabsContent">
    <!-- 1. Clean Architecture Tab -->
    <div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="clean-arch">
        <div class="card p-4">
            <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark border-bottom pb-2">Clean Architecture (Onion Pattern)</h5>
            <p class="text-muted">
                ApexCMMS separates concerns across four independent projects to ensure testability, maintainability, and zero domain pollution:
            </p>

            <div class="row g-3 mt-1">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100 p-3 bg-light border-start border-primary border-4">
                        <h6 class="fw-bold text-primary mb-1">ApexCMMS.Domain</h6>
                        <p class="small text-muted mb-2">The enterprise core with zero external framework dependencies.</p>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li><strong>Entities:</strong> <code>Asset</code>, <code>WorkOrder</code>, <code>SparePart</code>, <code>Department</code>, <code>AuditLog</code>, <code>ApplicationUser</code></li>
                            <li><strong>Enums:</strong> <code>AssetStatus</code>, <code>AssetCriticality</code>, <code>WorkOrderPriority</code>, <code>WorkOrderStatus</code></li>
                            <li><strong>Contracts:</strong> <code>BaseEntity</code>, <code>IAuditableEntity</code></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100 p-3 bg-light border-start border-info border-4">
                        <h6 class="fw-bold text-info mb-1">ApexCMMS.Application</h6>
                        <p class="small text-muted mb-2">Use cases, DTOs, and interface abstractions.</p>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li><strong>DTOs:</strong> Auth requests, Asset filters, Work order details, Inspection wizard state</li>
                            <li><strong>Interfaces:</strong> <code>IApplicationDbContext</code>, <code>ICurrentUserService</code>, <code>IJwtTokenService</code></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100 p-3 bg-light border-start border-warning border-4">
                        <h6 class="fw-bold text-warning mb-1">ApexCMMS.Infrastructure</h6>
                        <p class="small text-muted mb-2">Data persistence, external protocols, and security implementations.</p>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li><strong>EF Core:</strong> <code>ApplicationDbContext</code> configured with <code>Projects</code> schema</li>
                            <li><strong>Automated Auditing:</strong> ChangeTracker interceptor capturing JSON property diffs</li>
                            <li><strong>JWT Engine:</strong> <code>JwtTokenService</code> with cryptographic token rotation</li>
                            <li><strong>Seeder:</strong> <code>DbInitializer</code> generating departments, roles, users, and telemetry</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100 p-3 bg-light border-start border-success border-4">
                        <h6 class="fw-bold text-success mb-1">ApexCMMS.Web</h6>
                        <p class="small text-muted mb-2">Presentation boundary for human browsers and field mobile apps.</p>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li><strong>MVC Controllers:</strong> Razor view rendering, Anti-CSRF verification</li>
                            <li><strong>REST APIs:</strong> <code>AuthController</code>, <code>TechnicianApiController</code></li>
                            <li><strong>Session State:</strong> Distributed memory cache for multi-step inspection forms</li>
                            <li><strong>Middleware:</strong> <code>SecurityHeadersMiddleware</code> (Anti-clickjacking, CSP, XSS)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. Hybrid Auth Tab -->
    <div class="tab-pane fade" id="security">
        <div class="card p-4">
            <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark border-bottom pb-2">Dual-Authentication Security Engine</h5>
            <p class="text-muted">
                ApexCMMS provides both <strong>Cookie Authentication</strong> for desktop management portals and <strong>JWT Bearer Authentication</strong> for field mobile workers:
            </p>

            <div class="row g-4 mt-1">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <h6 class="fw-bold text-primary"><i class="bi bi-browser-chrome me-1"></i> Web UI: Secure Cookie Session</h6>
                    <ul class="small text-muted">
                        <li><strong>HttpOnly:</strong> Cookies are inaccessible via client-side JavaScript, preventing XSS session hijacking.</li>
                        <li><strong>SameSite=Lax:</strong> Strict isolation preventing Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF).</li>
                        <li><strong>Anti-Forgery Tokens:</strong> Automatic validation on all mutating POST/PUT/DELETE actions.</li>
                        <li><strong>Sliding Expiration:</strong> Renews active user sessions after 8 hours of activity.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <h6 class="fw-bold text-success"><i class="bi bi-phone me-1"></i> Mobile API: JWT Bearer & Refresh Token Rotation</h6>
                    <ul class="small text-muted">
                        <li><strong>HMAC-SHA256:</strong> Cryptographically signed JSON Web Tokens carrying <code>sub</code>, <code>role</code>, and <code>DepartmentId</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Short-lived Access Tokens:</strong> 60-minute lifetime reduces exposure window.</li>
                        <li><strong>Refresh Token Rotation:</strong> Every token exchange revokes the previous token and issues a new pair.</li>
                        <li><strong>Replay Attack Defense:</strong> If a revoked token is reused, the entire token family is immediately revoked.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. RBAC Tab -->
    <div class="tab-pane fade" id="rbac">
